  "protocol": "Stake DAO Votemarket",
  "name": "Stake DAO L1BlockOracleUpdater sender check bypass for chain 1",
  "summary": "L1BlockOracleUpdater.receiveMessage rejected a LaPoste message only when the source chain was not 1 and the sender was untrusted, so any Ethereum sender passed. The attacker sent a fake L1 block to the Arbitrum and Base updaters, which wrote it into the Votemarket oracles, then proved fabricated votes against a crafted header and claimed 54 Votemarket campaigns.",
